# Task 4 Report: Incremental Immutable Diagnosis Fact Cache

## Delivered files

- `core/pit_diagnosis/fact_cache.py`: session-at-a-time PIT materializer, checkpoint/resume, immutable SQLite finalization, and read-only cache reader.
- `core/pit_diagnosis/supplemental.py`: frozen institutional/group snapshots and explicit unavailable provider.
- `tests/test_pit_diagnosis_fact_cache.py`: offline PIT, resume, and identity coverage.

## Schema and provenance decisions

- SQLite has `metadata(key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT NOT NULL)` and normalized `session_facts`, keyed by `(bundle_sha256, rulebook_schema_version, symbol, session)`.
- Rows contain only session-visible OHLCV, prior price/volume facts, visible fundamental state, RS, pre-event base structure, market facts, supplemental evidence IDs, availability bits, and canonical row hashes. They contain no leader labels, experiment outcomes, agent decisions, raw payloads, or secrets.
- Checkpoint identity binds bundle digest/metadata source hashes, rulebook, partitions, supplemental identity, and schema. Checkpoints replace atomically; progress records are append-only and fsynced per completed session.
- The unavailable provider uses the fixed all-zero identity. Non-default providers require nonzero content identity and future-dated evidence fails closed.
- Finalization runs SQLite integrity and per-session membership-count checks, sets complete metadata, removes sidecars, atomically renames the partial file, and marks it read-only. Opening rehashes and uses SQLite `mode=ro` only.

